{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Er, the firstborn of Judah, was evil in the eyes of YHWH.</b> Scripture does not specify his transgression as it does regarding his brother, but states only that he died for his sin, to make known that this was not a punishment upon Judah for the selling of Joseph, for the deliverance was sustained through the sale, and there was no childlessness in the house of the fathers other than this one who was evil in the eyes of HaShem, for the seed of the righteous is blessed. And therefore Jacob mourned over his son for many days and refused to be comforted, for the matter was in his eyes a great punishment upon him, apart from his love for him:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:27.991727493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}